preferred-citation:
  type: generic
  title: "Improved Conditional Logistic Regression using Information in Concordant Pairs with Software"
  authors:
    - family-names: Kapelner
      given-names: Adam
    - family-names: Tennenbaum
      given-names: Jacob
  year: 2026
  doi: "10.48550/arXiv.2602.08212"
  url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.08212"
abstract: >
  bclogit fits conditional logistic regression models for matched
  case-control data that optionally incorporate information from
  concordant pairs (and a reservoir of additional controls) as an
  informative Bayesian prior, improving estimation of the discordant
  pairs' effects. The package also provides a vanilla clogit()
  implementation that runs 5-11x faster than survival::clogit().
